From 9757b161717b68d6c2d9911c46632a817856af51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:20:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: clear the ranged danger when Crush would kill the
 monster

borg_danger_one_kill() has two Crush adjustments: one in the melee part
and one in the ranged part.  Both test the same condition (the monster
has fewer hit points than four times the caster's level, is in view and
on a floor grid), but the ranged one cleared v1 -- the melee value the
first block had already cleared -- instead of v2.

So a monster that Crush would kill kept all of its ranged danger, and
borg_attack_aux_crush(), which values the spell as the drop in danger,
saw no benefit against any crushable monster that attacks from range.
A Necromancer with Crush did nothing against a weak mage or archer
shooting at it from a few steps away.

Clear v2 in the ranged block.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#66.
---
 src/borg/borg-danger.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-danger.c b/src/borg/borg-danger.c
index 11efe9f1a..c969c8f8f 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-danger.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-danger.c
@@ -2742,7 +2742,7 @@ int borg_danger_one_kill(
         if ((kill->power * (100 - kill->injury)) / 100 < borg.trait[BI_CLEVEL] * 4) {
             borg_grid* ag = &borg_grids[y9][x9];
             if (ag->info & BORG_VIEW && borg_cave_floor_grid(ag))
-                v1 = 0;
+                v2 = 0;
         }
     }
 
